  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 1, 'Before your next meeting or class, write down one point you would like to make, and keep the note where you can see it.'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 2, 'Pick one group you will be part of this week and name the smallest thing you could say there, like a simple "I agree."'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 3, 'Say one sentence out loud in the first five minutes of a meeting today, even if it is only a hello to the group.'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 4, 'At dinner with family or friends tonight, share one thing you noticed today before anyone asks you.'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 5, 'On a video call today, type one short comment or question in the chat instead of only listening.'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 6, 'Read tomorrow''s agenda tonight and jot one question you are curious about next to an item.'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 7, 'Practice one opening line aloud in the car or shower: "One thing I''d add is..." Say it three times at an easy pace.'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 8, 'When someone in a group makes a point you like, tell them so out loud: "That''s a good point, Sam."'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 9, 'Ask one clarifying question in a group today, such as "Can you say more about what you mean by that?"'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 10, 'Before you speak in any group today, take one slow breath out and let your shoulders drop.'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 11, 'After a meeting today, send a short follow-up note with one thought you had but did not say.'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 12, 'Use the raise-hand button on a video call once today, and wait to be called on.'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 13, 'In a group chat today, reply to a question with your honest opinion rather than only a reaction.'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 14, 'Notice who in your next meeting has not spoken yet, and simply note their name for now.'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 15, 'Tonight, write down one moment today when your voice was heard, however small.'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 16, 'At a party or gathering this week, ask the group one open question and listen to the answers.'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 17, 'When you speak today, say your first sentence a little slower than feels natural.'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 18, 'Sit where people can see you at your next meeting, near the middle of the table or with your camera on.'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 19, 'Build on someone else''s idea once today by starting with "And to add to that..."'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 20, 'Write a single sentence that sums up your view on a topic coming up this week, then read it aloud twice.'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 21, 'Offer to read the agenda or take the first item at a small meeting or club gathering this week.'),
  ('speaking-up-in-groups', 22, 'Before a class or session starts, say something to the person next to you so your voice is already warmed up.'),
